# The Elsewhere API (site/server.mjs). Leave this unset while developing: the
# app then uses the server on the computer running Expo (`npm run dev` in
# site/). Once the site is deployed, put its address in apps/mobile/.env:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-project.vercel.app
# To work on server code with a deployed address set, override it in
# .env.local with your computer's server, for example:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.20:3010

# Google Maps on iOS (see README): a key with "Maps SDK for iOS" enabled,
# restricted to iOS apps with the bundle ID app.elsewhere.mobile. Without it
# the map uses Apple Maps. Rebuild with `npx expo run:ios` after changing it.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_IOS_KEY=

# Crash reports (Sentry, src/lib/crash-reports.ts): the project's DSN, from
# Sentry → Project settings → Client keys. Without it nothing is sent.
# Release builds only; development builds never report.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# For readable stack traces, also set these and rebuild (SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN
# belongs in the build environment, not in a committed file):
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=
